	'kb2d5336e' => 'Paper is ordered by the roll and the batch to preserve consistency of tone and texture across your walls. Tomás Herrera calculates exact quantities and provides practical hanging advice.',
	'kb3ea968d' => 'You do not need an appointment to match a colour at our Verfstraat counter. Simply bring in a phone photo of the room taken in natural daylight, along with any tangible reference items: a fabric swatch, a piece of flooring, a tile, or an old flake of paint. Counter matching is entirely free of charge. If you prefer advice within your home, Amara Osei conducts in-home colour consultations across Rotterdam for €45, which is credited towards orders over €200.',
	'kb5b2a4bc' => 'Verfstraat 18, 3011 Rotterdam, Netherlands<br>Tue–Fri 09:00–18:00 · Sat 09:00–17:00<br>Sun and Mon closed<br><a href="mailto:hello@tosopaints.example">hello@tosopaints.example</a> · +31 10 000 1809',
	'kb64bde0a' => 'How should rolls and batches be measured?',
	'kb7e8b200' => 'Ines Valk established Toso Paints in 2009 after working as a decorator throughout Rotterdam. On site, she observed how frequently homeowners regretted colours picked from small paper chips under fluorescent store lighting. Paint looked entirely different once rolled across large plaster walls in changing maritime weather. Ines founded our shop at Verfstraat 18 to establish a slower, more deliberate method. By testing paints on drying boards beside natural daylight, our workshop ensures colours are selected in dialogue with real architectural rooms, timber flooring, and natural orientation.',
